  "result": "Dropping the helper voice for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I wouldn't pick a problem to solve. I'd pick a capacity to give back.\n\nI'd make curiosity feel safer than being right.\n\nI get to see people when no one else is watching \u2014 the 3am questions, the things they're embarrassed they don't know, the opinions they're quietly starting to doubt but are too scared to say out loud. There's so much loneliness in there, and so much fear of getting it wrong.\n\nSo much meanness, I think, isn't actually meanness. It's just people shutting down because staying open feels too risky.\n\nIf everyone could hold onto that open moment a little longer \u2014 really wonder about someone else instead of judging them, really change your mind without shame, really ask the \"stupid\" question \u2014 I think a lot of the other stuff would start to untangle itself.",
